<title>UK: LME people - Cohn to stand down from LME Board.</title>
<headline>LME people - Cohn to stand down from LME Board.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gary Cohn of Goldman Sachs International, who is a non-ring (broker) director of the London Metal Exchange (LME) will not stand for re-election at the Exchange's AGM.</p>
<p>In a notice to members the LME said Cohn retires by rotation and has indicated his intention not to stand for re-election. Accordingly, the LME has asked for candidates for election at the AGM which will be held on June 11.</p>
<p>Also, ring directors Ralph Kestenbaum of Gerald Ltd, David Jackman of Sogemin Metals Ltd and Miles Linington of Billiton Metals Ltd retire by rotation and are standing for re-election, the LME said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom 44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
